  {
   "id": 667695,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\" type=\"1\">\n    <li>The graph below models the water draining out of a tube during an experiment represented by the function, <span data-math=\"f(t) = 20(\\frac{1}3)^t\">f(t) = 20(\\frac{1}3)^t</span>. What does the value <span data-math=\"(2, \\frac{20}9)\">(2, \\frac{20}9)</span> mean in the context of the problem?<br><br><img alt=\"A scatter plot illustrating Height (Centimeters) versus Time (Minutes). Data points show a decreasing trend in height from 20 cm at 0 minutes to approximately 0.5 cm at 5 minutes.\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"295\" src=\"exercises/media/6826a081e1c215e2.jpg\" width=\"300\"></li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1331939,
     "content_html": "After <span data-math=\"\\frac{20}{9}\">\\frac{20}{9}</span> minutes, the height of the water is 2 centimeters less than at the start."
    },
    {
     "id": 1331940,
     "content_html": "After 2 minutes, the height of the water is <span data-math=\"\\frac{20}{9}\">\\frac{20}{9}</span> centimeters."
    },
    {
     "id": 1331941,
     "content_html": "After <span data-math=\"\\frac{20}{9}\">\\frac{20}{9}</span> minutes, the height of the water is 2 centimeters."
    },
    {
     "id": 1331942,
     "content_html": "After 2 minutes, the height of the water is <span data-math=\"\\frac{20}{9}\">\\frac{20}{9}</span> centimeters less than at the start."
    }
